{
  "_guide": {
    "standing": "a jab with the sharp end that bypasses half armor. Has a chance based on your luck to stack luck. With mining fatigue, becomes a hammer smash that deals increased posture damage.",
    "falling": "a downward swing that briefly pins. With mining fatigue, consumes it and creates a small shockwave that flings up blinding debris.",
    "sprinting": "downward swing while charging forward, drags the first enemy hit.",
    "guard counter": "slow wide swing that pins. At max spirit, follow up with a pull that drags mobs to you.",
    "throw": "consumes some spirit to throw a random stone type block. Basic stone shatters on impact, while luck and higher spirit give a chance to instead throw an ore that can either bounce or pierce, and either embed or fall to the ground. (By this construction, the only throw move that can trigger a pickup flourish is a lucky ore throw)",
    "pickup flourish": "raise the ore triumphantly, stacking haste for a semi long duration",
    "draw attack": "heavy sideways hammer smash that consumes mining fatigue. This is so pickaxe can be chained in to essentially animation cancel the hit recovery on other weapons."
  },
